## Device Capability Detection (Refactored)

### Current Issues
— `DeviceCapability` uses UA sniffing (`/Mobi|Android/i`) — **unreliable** on modern browsers
— No touch detection, no `maxTouchPoints` check
— Single call at init, no periodic re-check
— No `isMobile` public getter

### Fix Plan
1. Replace UA + `navigator.maxTouchPoints` + `screen.width/h` as mobile detection
2. Add `isMobile`, `isTouch` public getters
3. Add `screen` size check — `screen.width < 500` → force low tier
4. Keep `dpr` and `concurrency` as fallback only

### Implementation
`src/core/DeviceCapability.ts`
```ts
private isMobile = this.detectMobile()

private detectMobile(): boolean {
  const hasTouch = navigator.maxTouchPoints > 0
  const smallScreen = Math.min(screen.width, screen.height)
  const uaCheck = /Mobi|Android|Silicon/i.test(navigator.userAgent)
  
  // Mobile if touch AND (small screen OR UA match)
  return hasTouch && (smallScreen < 768 || uaCheck)
}
```

Replace `this.detectTier()` to use `this.isMobile` instead of UA string.

